    {
      "id": "47615689",
      "title": "What is Topological Sort?",
      "lectureOrder": 255,
      "videoOrder": 253,
      "sourceHash": "6bdb2eb0f512716d43c1022760dc21c3dbcf7d3db979fce474063e2f16976cbc",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 5.21,
          "end": 5.72,
          "en": "All right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.72,
          "end": 9.29,
          "en": "In this lecture we are going to learn a new topic which is called topological sort.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.32,
          "end": 10.31,
          "en": "By definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.31,
          "end": 11.57,
          "en": "Topological sorts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.6,
          "end": 18.83,
          "en": "Topological sort sorts given actions in a such way that if there is a dependency of one action on another,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.83,
          "end": 22.88,
          "en": "then dependent action always comes later than its parent action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.91,
          "end": 30.83,
          "en": "So the key concepts over here is that topological sort is only defined for directed graph with no cycles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 30.83,
          "end": 34.79,
          "en": "which means that it only works for directed acyclic graph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.79,
          "end": 40.25,
          "en": "If the graph has a cycle, then it's impossible to create valid topological ordering, and the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 40.25,
          "end": 46.58,
          "en": "of topological sort is a linear sequence of vertices that respects the dependencies defined by the edges",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 46.58,
          "end": 47.18,
          "en": "in the graph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 47.21,
          "end": 51.95,
          "en": "Now, initially, it might be a little bit confusing not to make this definition clear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 51.98,
          "end": 54.26,
          "en": "Let's look at the our morning schedule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.26,
          "end": 56.78,
          "en": "So first we do the morning exercise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.78,
          "end": 59.66,
          "en": "Then after doing the morning exercise we take a shower.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 59.69,
          "end": 61.46,
          "en": "Then we have a breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.46,
          "end": 62.39,
          "en": "Then we go to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.39,
          "end": 65.39,
          "en": "So here after shower we have a breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.39,
          "end": 69.12,
          "en": "But before having the breakfast we have to prepare the breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.12,
          "end": 76.41,
          "en": "So this means that this action of breakfast depends on other action where we need to prepare the breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.41,
          "end": 81.03,
          "en": "But before preparing the breakfast, we need to buy something for preparing the breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 81.03,
          "end": 82.02,
          "en": "So let's see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.02,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "We need to buy fruits.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 86.34,
          "en": "Then after buying the fruits we can prepare the breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.37,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "Now after preparing the breakfast we can have the breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "So as you can see, the breakfast itself depends on the prepare breakfast action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 93.66,
          "en": "So.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 96.78,
          "en": "So without buying fruit, we cannot prepare the breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.78,
          "end": 100.65,
          "en": "And without preparing the breakfast we cannot have the breakfast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.68,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "Then after preparing the breakfast we are going to wash the dishes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "Then after having the breakfast, we are going to continue to do work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "So hopefully with this daily routine you understand that what topological sort meaning?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "Now the problem over here is if all these actions are given and how we will identify the order of actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "that need to be done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "So we cannot go to work if we don't have the breakfast and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 125.85,
          "en": "So we need to identify all steps in order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.85,
          "end": 131.91,
          "en": "So to solve this problem, topological sorting helps us if we apply topological sort, it will identify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.91,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "the dependencies between these actions and will start from the parent and continue to the children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 141.99,
          "en": "So in our case, as I mentioned, first we do the exercise, then we take the shower and it continues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 142.29,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 142.29,
          "end": 146.28,
          "en": "Now let's look at the real graph and how this is working on real graph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.28,
          "end": 148.02,
          "en": "So let's say we have a graph like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 148.02,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "So in this case this is directed acyclic graph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 152.82,
          "en": "So we don't have any cycle over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.82,
          "end": 154.68,
          "en": "So it might seem that there is a cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "But as you can see from F we cannot go to the D.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.56,
          "end": 159.9,
          "en": "That's why this is directed edge over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.9,
          "end": 161.37,
          "en": "So there is no cycle over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.37,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "So take into account that for topological sort we can have more than one answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 169.11,
          "en": "So for example for this graph one answer can be like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.11,
          "end": 175.65,
          "en": "So first we need to do the a then b then c because c depends on a and d depends on b.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.65,
          "end": 180.6,
          "en": "So as you can see they come before these two vertices and it continues like now another solution can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 183.72,
          "en": "be like this b a, c, d, e, f, g.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 185.85,
          "en": "And another solution can be like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 185.85,
          "end": 189.09,
          "en": "And there is not only one solution for topological sort.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.12,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "So when we are applying the topological sort any graph we are going to use the stack data structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "So that's why I'm just going to put the stack data structure over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 198.93,
          "en": "So let's say we are starting from a.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.96,
          "end": 204.4,
          "en": "So the algorithm says that if a vertex depends on the current vertex, then we are going to that vertex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.4,
          "end": 208.03,
          "en": "And after going there we are going to come back to the current vertex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.03,
          "end": 211.78,
          "en": "So here from A we see that there is a node which is c depends on A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.81,
          "end": 213.64,
          "en": "So a is the current vertex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.64,
          "end": 215.56,
          "en": "Then we go to the that vertex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.56,
          "end": 217.15,
          "en": "So we are going to continue to the c.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.18,
          "end": 221.38,
          "en": "Now when we reach c we see that there is another vertex depends on c which is e.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 221.41,
          "end": 222.79,
          "en": "We will continue to this one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.79,
          "end": 226.9,
          "en": "Then here we see that there are two vertices depends on e, h and f.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.9,
          "end": 228.82,
          "en": "So first we will continue to h.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.85,
          "end": 233.59,
          "en": "Then when we reach the h we see that there is no any other vertex depends on h.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.59,
          "end": 236.26,
          "en": "So we are going to take h and insert into the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.29,
          "end": 237.91,
          "en": "Then we will come back one more time to e.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.94,
          "end": 241.36,
          "en": "We see that there is f which is not in the stack depends on E.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.36,
          "end": 246.13,
          "en": "So we are going to continue to F, and we see that g depends on f also.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246.13,
          "end": 249.28,
          "en": "So we are going to take g and insert into the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.31,
          "end": 250.45,
          "en": "Then we'll come back to F.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.48,
          "end": 253.21,
          "en": "We see that we have already put the g in the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.21,
          "end": 257.14,
          "en": "So we can easily go ahead and put the F to the stack over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.14,
          "end": 258.91,
          "en": "Then we will continue to do E.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.91,
          "end": 262.6,
          "en": "So you see that on E depends f and h.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.6,
          "end": 264.61,
          "en": "And both of them are inserted in the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.61,
          "end": 267.64,
          "en": "So we can go ahead and insert e also into the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 267.67,
          "end": 269.2,
          "en": "Then we'll continue to see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.23,
          "end": 271.33,
          "en": "So here again is applicable for C.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.36,
          "end": 272.98,
          "en": "C will be inserted to the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.01,
          "end": 274.48,
          "en": "Then we continue to a.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.51,
          "end": 277.39,
          "en": "So a depends on C and c is already in the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.39,
          "end": 279.64,
          "en": "So we can insert the A to the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.67,
          "end": 283.78,
          "en": "Now as you can see other vertices BD are left over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.78,
          "end": 284.98,
          "en": "So we will continue to be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.98,
          "end": 290.08,
          "en": "So b depends on d we will continue to d and d depends on f.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.08,
          "end": 293.38,
          "en": "But f is already visited which means that it's in the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.38,
          "end": 296.26,
          "en": "So we are going to take D and insert into the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.29,
          "end": 300.97,
          "en": "Then we are just going to go to back to B and insert that one also to the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.97,
          "end": 305.5,
          "en": "Now we know that in stack the last one that is inserted will come out first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 305.53,
          "end": 307.93,
          "en": "So I'm just going to pop out the all elements from the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.93,
          "end": 311.74,
          "en": "So the order is going to be the way that they are removed from the stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 311.74,
          "end": 313.33,
          "en": "So this is going to be our order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 313.33,
          "end": 319.87,
          "en": "So as you can see first we are doing a, then with D then before F we have E over here we are continuing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 319.9,
          "end": 323.17,
          "en": "A, C, D, e, F, G and h.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 323.17,
          "end": 326.89,
          "en": "So with this I have shown you the logic behind the topological sort.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 326.92,
          "end": 331.54,
          "en": "So the logic behind the topological sort and how it works with a stack data structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.57,
          "end": 337,
          "en": "Now in the next lecture we are going to look at the code and debug it and see how this is working.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
